Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:13.949
Pride, Greed, Wrath, Envy, Lust, Gluttony
and Sloth.

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:19.830
The Seven Capital Vices or Seven Deadly Sins.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:26.259
Succumb to any of these you’ll end up in
your very own version of the Divine Comedy.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:32.020
Being guided through hell and climbing out
through satan's nutsack.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:37.050
Or maybe not who knows, I’m no expert.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.430
It’s likely most of have heard of the Seven
Deadly Sins in some capacity.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:47.850
When we discussed Peter Binsfeld classification
of demons each of the seven demon princes

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.590
of hell represented one of these seven deadly
sins.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:58.239
This became a fairly common way for historians
and demonologists to personify and create

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:01.600
a taboo around these ideas.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:11.550
Today we’ll take a look at what these sins
actually meant and why they were so deadly.

